%description:

Tcp.frtoEnabled:off -- the response to the spurious timeout stays.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "F-RTO spurious-RTO detection (RFC 5682, SACK-enhanced; Linux
tcp_frto=2)".

The classes: off (false, the default) and on (true, the value of LinuxTcp). The code:
Rfc6675Recovery::onRexmitTimeout() opens the detection; at the first ACK of new data after the
timeout, Rfc6675Recovery::segmentsAcked() and processFrtoEpisode() undo the response to the
timeout when the ACK acknowledges data that was sent only once. F-RTO needs SACK. This test separates "off" from "on".

Host under test: host1, without the tail loss probe and the undo of losses (preconditions:
they act on the same timeout), which sends three segments; the round trip is 40 ms. The tap delays each ACK of
data of host2 in the first 0.5 s by 1.5 s, so the timer of host1 expires, although host2
has all the data. host1 retransmits the first segment; the ACK of the copy acknowledges all
three segments, two of them sent only once. Observation: level 3, at 2.5 s, the threshold is still the one of the timeout, 2 * SMSS =
2920 bytes.

%# parameter: Tcp.frtoEnabled
%# class: off
%# value: false
%# key: *.host1.tcp.frtoEnabled
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpFrtoEnabledOff")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host2").filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && tcp.ackNo > {isn} + 1").delay(1.5).within(0.5)
                     .describe("each ACK of data of host2 in the first 0.5 s: 1.5 s late"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("numRtos").describe("the timeout of host1").within(2.0))
        .act(action().at(2.5)
                 .describe("the threshold at 2.5 s")
                 .assertModule("host1.tcp.conn-*", "state.ssthresh == 2920"));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpFrtoEnabledOff compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.frtoEnabled = false    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 4344B
*.host1.tcp.tlpEnabled = false
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpFrtoEnabledOff: PASS
